"Tony": `tony himself is not very recognized by anyone, having completed no major achievement for such possibilities. he is more overshadowed by his older brother, who plays in a rather popular rock band. unfortunate for him... i wouldn't blame you if you didn't know him either.

however, tony doesn't let that be an issue. he has a lot of connections, despite his arrogant attitude. most notably is his friendship with ms. doe, a well known great sharpshooter. i think everyone knows her, no need to detail anything. though seemingly, they have been interacting less as of recently.

he goes around districts, competing in golfing contests. though only at the middle point of his career, he's been starting to gather up significant wins, unlike before. he was a bit laughed at when he started, losing a lot, but i think that's how it is when you're new to something.

he is trying to make a name for himself in the golfing industry, using his trusty golf club given to him by his father. not bad at all i'd say, jealous of him even.`,

"Robinson": `the robinson family is very known for their services done all over the city. rarely do they appear in the news headlines of doing something memorable but if you stuck long enough in the city, like me, you'd know them. they're a nice bunch.

consisting of four members, originally five but the mother passed away a few years back. now it's just the three brothers and the father. after this event, they went a bit quiet for some time but eventually they opened up again, helping people again.

despite their good parts, the brothers are also a very messy trio. they get into trouble sometimes but they're pretty young, i can understand it and they really want to make a band. the father says that their determination to make one is incredible but they never quite did it. probably time constraints.`,

"Rogue Sig Boy": `Previously mentioned, most of the unemployeds traversing utilize melee weapons as to not waste precious resources. However, when trusted by the leader, you're given a gun. So, usually people with a gun are ordered to stay more inside locations, waiting for anyone that enters to catch them off guard and bring a quick end.

Similar to the previous ranks, these people are also unprofessional in utilizing weaponry properly, so they're not too intimidating. But don't be completely ignorant of their potential either.`,

"Rogues": `After the rebellion, many split into many factions, groups or went off alone. For those who are unemployed but willing to get into one, which is the rogue citizens, the only one that is available, they must show their dedication and craftsmanship to this through several possible methods. The most basic, however, is prove you're combat worthy.

Most of these unemployed civilians utilize melees, as they're much more common to find and are more brawn than brains. So to say, them bringing such a close quarter weapon to a fight, which most of the time will be a gunfight, is not the greatest choice. But they have to work with what they have. Usually, another experienced civilian will train the others so they don't perish. The blind leading the blind.

There is some sort of hierachy to this however, the ones with melees are typically taken as the lower ranks. The ones with guns are higher ranks, except one: the king. His appearance is obvious, he leads this... "faction" of unemployeds. This king is usually not seen though, hiding alongside his bodyguards. The loot from other people, brought by the lower ranks, is given to the king for inspection and to be used by him.

As scary as this all sounds, they're really just untrained people running around with weapons. Anyone more experienced could take care of them.`,

"Sapling": `They're often mistaken as normal plants, but for some reason.. these things can walk and they're incredibly aggressive. Many people who tried to sneak into the witch's cottage often gets stopped by them before they could get in any deeper.

Nobody really knows how these things are made, and the witch herself isn't very communicative, so we'll probably never get to recreate a walking plant as well.`,

"Rogue Lead": `The leader of the unemployeds. You won't see him outside much or, if anything, at all. Could this be because he's scared or maybe it's not worth going outside? Who knows. Although, just in case, he has bodyguards to protect him. Not the greatest bodyguards but it'll have to do. Mostly.

He may look threatening but like every other unemployed, he's not an expert at this. Probably his first time leading so many people all at once. But he definitely does not seem like he's stressed out by this, so that shows some determination. Some respect him, some laugh at him. Those who laugh? Well, as tough as this sounds, he mostly doesn't care. Why would he go after 'garbage' as he says?

Takes a lot of pride in his rank, making quite a hassle out of small situations sometimes just to look tough. This is just to intimidate outsiders, making them believe that he is a strict, brutal leader. It's not quite the same in reality but he thinks it'll do. Somehow, people look up to him.

Although all of the members give him all the loot found, it's never something really great. Especially since it's in the city that has been looted by everyone. He usually tells them to find better loot. They never do.`,

